How to read the isolation:
  * If CSS-X (true H) stays ~flat/floored across k while Direct CSS (true H)
    drops toward the oracle as k grows -> the CSS-X failure is CONSTRUCTION
    (original axes cannot span the rotated subspace), NOT H-estimation error,
    since both use a perfect H.
  * Compare (true H) vs (est H) rows at the same k to see how much the poor
    rotated EGOP estimate degrades each method on top of the construction limit.
